 {
  "default_value": null,
  "doc_type": "Full and Final Settings",
  "docstatus": 0,
  "doctype": "Property Setter",
  "doctype_or_field": "DocField",
  "field_name": "long_text_pwoi",
  "is_system_generated": 0,
  "modified": "2026-04-27 00:37:04.351880",
  "module": null,
  "name": "Full and Final Settings-long_text_pwoi-default",
  "property": "default",
  "property_type": "Text",
  "row_name": null,
  "value": "End of Service Gratuity Logic (If-Then Rules)\n1. Activation Rules:\n\nIF the Company is located in \"Saudi Arabia\" AND the Employment Type is \"Permanent\":\n\nTHEN the system automatically calculates the gratuity.\n\nOTHERWISE:\n\nTHEN the gratuity amount will remain 0.\n\n2. Calculation Brackets (Article 84):\n\nIF service duration is 5 years or less:\n\nTHEN the award is half a month's wage for each year.\n\nIF service duration is more than 5 years:\n\nTHEN the award is one full month's wage for every year beyond the first five.\n\n3. Resignation Adjustments (Article 85):\n\nIF the Reason of Leaving is \"Resignation\":\n\nIF service is less than 2 years → THEN Payout is 0.\n\nIF service is 2 to 5 years → THEN Payout is 1/3 of the award.\n\nIF service is 5 to 10 years → THEN Payout is 2/3 of the award.\n\nIF service is 10 years or more → THEN Payout is Full (100%).\n\nIF the Reason of Leaving is \"Termination\" or \"End of Contract\":\n\nTHEN the employee receives the Full Award (100%) regardless of the above percentages."
 },
