  "row_name": null,
  "value": "1"
 },
 {
  "default_value": null,
  "doc_type": "Full and Final Settings",
  "docstatus": 0,
  "doctype": "Property Setter",
  "doctype_or_field": "DocField",
  "field_name": "saudi_labor",
  "is_system_generated": 0,
  "modified": "2026-04-27 00:37:04.409420",
  "module": null,
  "name": "Full and Final Settings-saudi_labor-default",
  "property": "default",
  "property_type": "Text",
  "row_name": null,
  "value": "Saudi End of Service Gratuity\n\nThis system calculates gratuity automatically during Full and Final Statement based on Saudi Labor Law.\n\nCalculation applies only when:\n\n• Company is in Saudi Arabia  \n• Employment Type = Permanent  \n• Reason of Leaving is valid\n\n----------------------------------\n\nService Period Calculation\n\nThe system calculates service duration from:\n\nJoining Date → Relieving Date\n\nAs per Saudi Labor Law, gratuity is based on total completed service period including proportional partial years.\n\n----------------------------------\n\nGeneral Calculation Rule (Article 84)\n\nFor the first 5 years of service:\n\n• Half month wage for each year\n\nFor service above 5 years:\n\n• Full month wage for each additional year\n\n----------------------------------\n\nResignation Rule (Article 85)\n\nIf employee resigns:\n\n• Less than 2 years = No entitlement  \n• 2 to less than 5 years = One Third of gratuity  \n• 5 to less than 10 years = Two Thirds of gratuity  \n• 10 years or more = Full gratuity\n\n----------------------------------\n\nTermination / End of Contract\n\nIf service ends by employer termination or contract completion:\n\n• Full gratuity applies according to Article 84\n\n----------------------------------\n\nSalary Basis\n\nThe system uses the employee’s latest wage including fixed salary components as required by Saudi Labor Law.\n\n----------------------------------\n\nSystem Result\n\nAfter calculation, gratuity is added automatically to the Payables table.\n\nAny update in dates, salary, or leaving reason will recalculate the amount automatically."
 },
